# ── NeedMap AI  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file is an example. Almost everything is optional.
# Secrets (URLs, keys) live in Google Secret Manager, never here.
# Service account JSON is auto-detected at backend/service-account.json.
# 
# To run locally:
#   1. Place your service-account.json in backend/
#   2. Run: python3 create_all_secrets.py  (creates secrets in Secret Manager)
#   3. That's it — no secrets in .env needed.
#
# These overrides are only for local development or edge cases:
#
# APP_NAME=NeedMap AI
# APP_VERSION=0.1.0
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
# JWT_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host/db   (overrides Secret Manager)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...                              (overrides Secret Manager)
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/sa.json (overrides auto-detect)
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com             (CORS)
# SQLALCHEMY_ECHO=true                            (debug SQL queries)
# RUN_MIGRATIONS=true                             (run DB migrations at startup)